From 3250fb75d4d245686572de5e08cef89fc69ef5b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:44:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: add the BCM2835 ARM timer

The ARM side timer of the BCM2835 and its successors was an
unimplemented device: it read as zero and never interrupted.  Plan 9
uses it to hand work from its USB FIQ handler to an IRQ handler and
reads its free running counter for interrupt timing; with it missing
USB transfers completed only when something else interrupted.

Implement it after chapter 14 of the BCM2835 ARM Peripherals
document: a 16 or 32 bit down counter with a load and a reload
register, a predivider and a prescaler, raising ARM interrupt 0 when
it reaches zero, and a free running counter with its own prescaler,
both counting the APB clock, 250 MHz unless set otherwise.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
---
 hw/arm/bcm2835_peripherals.c         |  14 +-
 hw/timer/bcm2835_armtmr.c            | 284 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/timer/meson.build                 |   2 +-
 hw/timer/trace-events                |   5 +
 include/hw/arm/bcm2835_peripherals.h |   3 +-
 include/hw/timer/bcm2835_armtmr.h    |  37 ++++
 6 files changed, 342 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hw/timer/bcm2835_armtmr.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/timer/bcm2835_armtmr.h

